INTRODUCTION
Poor biowaste management releases potent greenhouse gases (GHG) such as methane (CH4), carbon dioxide (CO2), and nitrous oxide (N2O), which accelerate global warming and drive climate change (Hajam et al. 2023). Agriculture accounts for approximately 12% of global greenhouse emissions, equivalent to 5.87 Gt CO2-eq. Over 65% of these emissions originate
