Data analysis
The total cumulative emissions at the end of day 15 were presented in a tabular format, as they represented overall trends during the bioconversion process. To enhance reliability, emission values from each treatment were averaged across replicates to allow meaningful comparisons across substrates. The statistical analysis of cumulative gas recorded in ppm for each substrate was conducted in RStudio (version R-4.3.3) using the ggplot2 package for graphical representation. A oneway ANOVA (Analysis of Variance) was performed at a significance level of α = 0.05 to test whether mean emissions differed significantly among the control and treated substrates, assuming that the data met the requirements of normality and homogeneity of variances. The carbon-to-nitrogen (C/N) ratio was calculated from the elemental analysis data using the measured %C and %N values. The C/N ratio is a key parameter influencing microbial activity, nitrogen mineralization,
